{
  "dom_id": "step-q46070",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A factory with $150$ machines produces $600\\,000$ baseball balls weekly. To determine the number of balls produced by a machine on average, the owner of the factory uses the formula\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{b}{m},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is the number of balls produced by the factory weekly, and $m$ is the number of machines in the factory.\n\nWhat is an appropriate measurement unit for $P?$",
  "worked_solution": "We are solving for measurement units, so we can ignore the quantities $150$ and $600\\,000.$ They do not matter, if we are just solving for units.\n\nSince $b$ represents $\\text{balls}$ and $m$ represents $\\text{machines},$ the appropriate measurement unit for $P=\\frac{b}{m}$ is $\\frac{\\text{balls}}{\\text{machines}}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
